{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788582590447553001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"exorcismal-tokophobic-agama","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a90fc093d005d78061310417dbeda0ee482d8646ed94d27457eef8b3ee5c28a7","event_uuid":"f723f2aa-3642-428c-9108-39a9e55bfca0","position":{"commit_sha":"574a46cdc4a96931245ac8df49caddf465d164ad","position":"1788573670114135001-f723f2aa-3642-428c-9108-39a9e55bfca0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"175dcdb8904d94514ca4b54d37014a310041ae3d2c32f02612bcdf3d78ea32b5","event_uuid":"f81bd534-04c0-4298-bfa7-f4d3908e3fd6","position":{"commit_sha":"bf0b70679a6a7f5ec43f11b3941775dd1c88172f","position":"1788573685842617001-f81bd534-04c0-4298-bfa7-f4d3908e3fd6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788573670114135001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f81bd534-04c0-4298-bfa7-f4d3908e3fd6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9183-aaae-667d-45e6"}],"description":"## The trap\n\nCorrecting an acceptance criterion on an already-reviewed ticket can make the ticket\n**unclosable without a prose rewrite**, because two independent mechanisms compose badly:\n\n1. Editing description TEXT invalidates the plan-review attestation (`stale-material`), so the\n   close gate refuses and demands a fresh `review-plan`.\n2. `review-plan` refuses admission for a description above `verify.max_ticket_description_chars`\n   (8,000).\n\nSo if the description is already near the cap, ANY correction that adds characters pushes it over,\nand the re-review that the close now requires becomes inadmissible.\n\n## Observed, 2026-09-05, on `9183-aaae-667d-45e6` (S2 of epic 6202)\n\nThe ticket's AC4 read \"A validated `daemon.json` change on a live daemon reloads Docker, never\nrestarts.\" That specifies behaviour that cannot work — dockerd's SIGHUP reload does not apply\n`builder.gc`, which the implementation documents and deliberately refuses. Correcting the AC to\nmatch reality took the description from **7,994 to 8,088 chars**, six characters of headroom\nconsumed and 88 over.\n\nResult: `rebar transition ... closed` refused with `stale-material`, and the prescribed remedy\n(\"Run `rebar review-plan` separately, then retry close\") would itself have refused on admission.\nRecovered by compressing the correction to 90 characters and relying on a ticket comment to carry\nthe reasoning — total 7,998.\n\n## Why this is worth recording rather than shrugging at\n\nDescriptions cluster just under the cap, because authors write until the limit stops them. That\nmakes \"already near the cap\" the COMMON case, not an edge case, so the trap is reachable by any\nagent that later finds a factually wrong AC. The pressure it applies is in the wrong direction:\nit makes deleting the explanation of a correction the cheapest way out, exactly when a correction\nis the thing most worth explaining.\n\nBoth mechanisms are individually correct and should be kept. `stale-material` is right — the plan\ndid change. The admission cap is right — it bounds review cost. Only their composition is hostile.\n\n## Not yet root-caused; possible directions, none endorsed\n\n- Exempt the Acceptance Criteria block from the admission character count (it is the part a\n  reviewer most needs and the part corrections land in).\n- Let the close gate's `stale-material` refusal distinguish a correction that only REMOVES or\n  REWORDS a criterion from one that adds scope, as it already distinguishes checkbox ticks (which\n  are correctly normalised out of the fingerprint).\n- Report remaining headroom in the `rebar edit` success line, not only when the cap is breached,\n  so the trap is visible before it closes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The interaction is root-caused: confirm both mechanisms fire as described, and establish\n      how many current tickets sit within (say) 200 chars of the cap, to size the exposure.\n- [ ] Correcting a wrong AC on a reviewed, near-cap ticket no longer requires deleting prose to\n      stay admissible — by whichever of the directions above survives review.\n- [ ] A regression test drives the composed path end to end: reviewed ticket at cap-minus-epsilon\n      -> AC text correction -> close, and asserts it does not deadlock on admission.\n- [ ] Whatever changes, `stale-material` still fires on a genuine plan change and the admission\n      cap still bounds review cost — neither guard is weakened to buy the ergonomics.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4bd0-b2da-a641-4e5a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Correcting a wrong AC on a near-cap reviewed ticket is a trap: the text edit invalidates the attestation, and the re-review the close then demands refuses on the 8000-char admission cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f723f2aa-3642-428c-9108-39a9e55bfca0","f81bd534-04c0-4298-bfa7-f4d3908e3fd6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788582590447553001,"uuid":"601c64c0-e620-47cf-aa36-a6af3c334060"}